# Harden the Docker build context against common local leak vectors.
# New for this port (the pinned dmac-assistant source did not carry a
# .dockerignore of its own -- its Dockerfile relied on the repo-root
# .dockerignore via `context: ..`); adapted from
# docker/bedrock-proxy/.dockerignore's pattern (PLAN-7 Task 4 precedent) for
# this port's docker/ns-sidecar/ context root.
#
# OI-3: the sidecar holds no credentials of its own -- its only env is
# NEXTSEEK_BASE_URL, SIDECAR_STAGING_DIR, SIDECAR_WS_PORT. Per-user
# credentials arrive per-request inside the WS envelope, never via env or a
# baked-in file. These guards exclude the upstream local-dev env overlay
# files (local-nextseek*.env) and the upstream standalone compose fragment,
# neither of which this port carries or wires (later tasks 13-15 own
# compose wiring).
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage*
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.prod
**/.env.dev
local-nextseek*.env
docker-compose.yml
**/credentials.json
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/id_rsa
**/id_rsa.*
.git
.venv
